# Where accounts and auth-gateway send traces and metrics, or that they send none.
# The platform delivers exactly one of two answers, and a process that gets neither
# refuses to start rather than guess:
#
#   TELEMETRY_STATE=available   the cell has a collector. Also sets
#                               OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT to its OTLP/gRPC address,
#                               e.g. http://otel-collector.otel-collector.svc.cluster.local:4317
#                               (http:// is plaintext because the mesh supplies mTLS;
#                               https:// is TLS).
#   TELEMETRY_STATE=absent      the cell has none. Also sets TELEMETRY_ABSENT_REASON to
#                               say why.
#
# The state decides. A cell's values override these defaults one key at a time, so a
# cell that sets `available` and an endpoint still carries the reason below; the
# process ignores the key its state does not use and logs that once.
#
# A local run has no cell, so it has no collector: traces go to wool's stdout tracer
# and metrics are not exported. Logs always go to stdout.
TELEMETRY_STATE=absent
TELEMETRY_ABSENT_REASON=A local run has no cell collector; traces go to the stdout tracer and metrics are not exported.
